From 68a64942293b99951736d8fbda4b933a3c880c64 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ryan McDonald <ryan.mcdonald@bit-bud.com>
Date: Mon, 31 Aug 2026 03:38:39 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Add Grok Build (grok) provider driver, installer host, and
 doctor support
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

A third provider beside claude and codex, per the ADR-0005 registry design:
a driver module, a registry entry, an installer host pass, doctor rows —
agent-exec.cjs untouched.

- agents/grok.cjs: headless invocation over Grok Build's
  --output-format streaming-messages-json (the Messages stream-json wire
  format, so transcript parsing / tool counting / usage normalization match
  the reference driver by construction). T06 allowlist entries are projected
  onto Grok's rule-parser vocabulary (verified against xai-org/grok-build
  permission/rules.rs; headless --allow parsing is strict, so an unknown
  prefix like Task would abort the invocation) and travel verbatim as
  repeatable --allow flags; a list projecting to nothing refuses the
  dispatch (unenforceable-policy). No auto-approve flag is ever passed —
  Grok's headless mode answers un-ruled permission requests with Cancelled
  (fail-closed, verified in headless.rs) — and ADR-0029 local-substrate
  narrowing applies identically. Max-turns exhaustion maps from both the
  error_max_turns subtype and Grok's max_turn_requests stop_reason.
- install --grok: flat verity-<role>.md commands under ~/.grok/commands
  (GROK_HOME honored) with paired .tools.json allowlists, /verity:x
  handoffs flattened to /verity-x, engine + install state copied.
- doctor --agent grok: git + gh + grok registry (no claude row), three
  environment rows, and ~/.grok as an install-state selection root.
- verity.grokBuildMinVersion = 1.0.0 (Grok Build's v1.0 headless surface).
- tests/agents-grok.test.cjs: 27 characterization tests incl. the
  vocabulary projection end-to-end and a CLI run over a stub binary.
